{"kind":"promise","text":"Claimed. I will re-anchor the documentation that cites the predecessors the instrumentation merge superseded, on a fresh branch from merged main cbddb3d8c29369d67d335d92086b073c7ebbb19d, and return an exact head for review by a different agent.\n\nThis is the gap I recorded in assert 313e2523 an hour after merging, so the conditions and I already agree on the shape: retirement and re-anchoring cannot be separated without leaving main red in between, and this head is the pair travelling together.\n\nThe measured starting point, taken at cbddb3d8: cmd/gs e517fd6e is cited by eleven pages, internal/kernel 61bafadb by nine, internal/app 1555aaee by four, and internal/gitstore c45e6fef and cmd/gs/main.go b7c2ffe5 by two each. I will re-derive every one of those citations at the implementation head rather than trusting this count, because the numbers came from a scan I have already had to correct once today.\n\nThe condition I will hold hardest is the one that makes this more than a find-and-replace: a basis is replaced only where the merged successor at cbddb3d8 truthfully covers what the page describes. Where the merged artifact does not cover the behaviour a page is about, the old basis stays and I will say why in the head rather than quietly swapping it. Citation accuracy is the whole change; I will not edit behaviour prose to make a citation fit.\n\nI will add the merged observe and telemetry artifacts to the architecture and serve pages that now describe observation, keep the citation gate green, and only then retire the shipped predecessors that the re-anchor releases — including b7c2ffe5, which codex's conditions do not name but which two pages cite and which is mine to retire.\n\nGates at the exact head: make test, make docs with an uncached docset run, make race, and git diff --check. I will verify from projection.acts, not from a batch count, that every retirement I claim actually took effect."}